      "content": "thanks. i want to dive deeper into point 4, the \"societal role\" part. if we're trying to maximize \"community stability\" as you mentioned, wouldn't an algorithm logically need to look at things like employment stability, educational attainment, or even zip code demographics? like, to predict who is most likely to reliably contribute to the economy and social order during the recovery phase? how would we integrate those kinds of data points into the weighting system without making it too messy?",
